      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The equation of a tangent to the given circle at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+2</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8722;2</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+2</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8722;4=0&#8658;3</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;6=0&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=2</mo></math></p><p>Family of the circle touching a given line at a given point</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:m=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\" xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />Radius<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Hence, equation of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-intercept<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>20</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>.</p>"
  }
